# NOTE: the www → apex canonical redirect that used to live here was
# removed. Cloudflare's newer Workers Static Assets deploy path (which this
# project uses) rejects _redirects rules with an absolute/host-based source
# URL ("Only relative URLs are allowed") — that syntax only worked on
# classic Cloudflare Pages. Host-level redirects like www → apex now need
# to be set up in the Cloudflare dashboard instead: Rules → Redirect Rules
# → create a rule matching hostname equals "www.solahairsalon.com",
# redirecting to "https://solahairsalon.com/${1}" (or a static target),
# status 301. See the README's "Non-canonical redirect" section for the
# exact steps.
#
# This file is kept as a placeholder for any future path-only (relative)
# redirects, which are still fully supported here — e.g.:
#   /old-page /new-page 301
